how did hobo jack from american pickers  get his nickname especially since he  seems to own most of a town and what  about those rumors he died keep watching  to find out all about him  history's american pickers is jam-packed  with colorful characters working their  hardest to get the best deals possible  on cars collectibles and other  high-priced items among the most beloved  in the show's rogues gallery is hobo  jack a nickname for antiquer jack sophia  the cheerful native of litchfield  illinois owns a lot of property in his  small rural town and tends to pan up the  most interesting things for host mike  wolfe to pick through and ultimately buy  from him sophia is skinny bearded  gray-haired and has a penchant for  breaking into tune and playing the  guitar thus far he's only appeared twice  on the show in season two's hobo jack  and season six is the return of hobo  jack but those two appearances won him a  lot of fans thanks to his steely skills  at the negotiating table it's perhaps  not surprising to learn that there's  much more than meets the eye when it  comes to hobo jack  american pickers has previously come  under fire for being a hair less than  fully authentic so it's perhaps not a  big shock to learn that jackson fear  currently lives a life that has little  in common with jojobas according to the  herald weekly in real life sapir  actually owns quite a bit of property on  which he's got a nice and comfortable  home and he is seen regularly bidding on  big ticket items and auctions all of my  life i've been collecting remnants of  the victorian era so you might not spy  the spry collector riding the rails but  you're likely to encounter him in places  such as the wayside antique mall and  other locales around his illinois  hometown while this revelation may  disappoint some hobo jack fans it's  worth noting that he's never been  anything less than 100 percent honest  about his point of origin video bob  whiteside who runs saphir's official  website is perfectly frank about the  multi-hyphenates collegiate background  and he speaks of his moneyed youth as  well a profile published in the  telegraph in 2015 also revealed that  saphir is the son of artist and sculptor  dorothy o young as sapir told the  telegraph my mother discouraged me from  becoming an artist because she said the  main way to make a living with art was  by teaching and she knew i was too shy  and introverted for that the article  also explained that sophia's parents  wouldn't fund his art school education  so he ended up paying his own way at the  washington university school of fine  arts saphir then reportedly spent years  traveling before buying property and  settling down in litchfield  hobo jack saphir isn't just a collector  he's also an author with multiple  published works and a musician with a cd  in circulation according to his official  website he's released three books to  date the latest of these is 2015's  amazing adventures of the [ __ ] prince  perth's official synopsis this book  contains very controversial opinions  about health animal rights human rights  government and injustice many of these  discussions are with a toad safire's  other works include the 2008 novel time  in a box which focuses on the journeys  of patches the dog and backwards the  railroad bum who becomes separated when  patches leaves their life to go soul  searching saphir also authored get a  horse a unique collection of early  automotive humor from turn of the  century magazines in 1989. additionally  saphir produced an album called the best  of backwoods hobo jack original songs by  an american picker saphir not only  writes and sings his own songs but he  also plays guitar harmonica and banjo  hobo jack apparently isn't saphir's  moniker of choice his unforgettable  nickname came from american pickers host  mike wolf in fact on his official  website zaphir bills himself as  backwoods jack forgoing the hobo  entirely in 2011 it was revealed that  sapir gained the name backwoods jack due  to the locale of his cabin safire's  collaborator bob whiteside explained in  a youtube video buzz potter and captain  dingo asked me about who jack really was  and a little about him i answered he  lives by himself on a winding road in  the backwoods they both smiled and said  that's it backwoods jack every hair of  his beard he was so interesting to look  at whiteside also claims that the  history channel came up with the hobo  jack nickname not wolf in a note on his  official facebook page saphir confirmed  whiteside's story and added that he'd  been performing his backwoods jack for  10 years at hobo festivals before  receiving it as his official hobo road  name at marquette iowa during a  gathering anyway you slice it backwoods  jack is a name that comes by honestly  according to the telegraph saphir lives  in a cabin with two dogs on his property  and the structure lacks running water or  electricity he does however use a  generator when he needs it  hobo jack sapir began collecting things  as a child he told traveling adventures  of a farm girl i can't explain why i  collect i remember around seven walking  home from school and looking for  treasure which i never found i just have  a treasure hunter mentality saphir's  favorite things to collect are classic  cars and car parts as he told the  telegraph i've owned probably 100 cars  in my life and i still have 30 of them  he also makes money restoring and  selling vehicles a hobby which  originally caused friends to suggest he  contacted the american pickers producers  american pickers has been dogged by  rumors that one of its cast members has  died on more than one occasion for  instance when frank fritz left the show  several websites circulated false rumors  that he'd passed away then in 2016 the  telegraph posted a bogus notice that  jack sapir had passed away to their  facebook page it's since been  immortalized in a screencap on saphir's  official website he responded in a  statement joking how many people get to  read their own obituary he also included  a modified quote from author mark twain  writing the report of my death was an  exaggeration happened to hobo jack  we died in the jungle  while sapir definitely isn't dead he  might be considering spending more time  smelling the roses according to the  telegraphs of fear expressed interest in  moving to san francisco where his  daughter lives but regardless of whether  he's living in the middle of the country  or on the west coast american pickers  fans will always root for their beloved  hobo  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite reality stars are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one
 

